From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:15:17 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 44/51] Plutonium: the app is Hydra

In Plutonium, T3 Code's web app is the Hydra shell. It names itself Hydra
(the page title, the sidebar, the welcome wizard, messages it sends, the
default theme, and settings and errors that mean this app), and it has a
mark of its own (three heads on one body) in place of T3's wordmark and
icons. Text about T3 Code itself keeps T3 Code's name: its desktop and
mobile apps, T3 Connect, the `t3` CLI, the theme file format, versions,
and its privacy and license notices.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
